WEBVTT

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.620
Thank you very much!

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.380
Let's meet again!

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.110
Please keep supporting us!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.720
Earphones is the best!

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.360
Where... am I?

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.470
Who... am I?

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.080
You are Ichinose Futaba-san.
You are still the lowest level of seiyuu.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.040
Lowest... But our concert was full...

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.150
Don't act proud just because
you had one concert-koro.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.110
The most important event of your
seiyuu life will be happening soon.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.570
Do you remember-koro?

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.810
O-Of course I do! Sir!

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.240
Then stop spacing out and get to work-koro!

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.730
Yes, sir! Work... work...

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.740
But today's work is just your part-time job.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.830
Futaba-chan, you've been busy recently, huh?

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.830
I was worried that you'd quit at this rate.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.420
Don't worry...

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.170
Earphones will never end!

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.560
Then, let's do it like we usually do
and have Rin-chan give the info...

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.270
Futaba, what did I say just now?

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.570
Huh? Did you say something just now?

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.990
Not, "did you say something?"!
I asked you what I just said!

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.860
U-Um...

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.600
Ow!

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.570
Futaba! You're spacing out too much!

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.280
Oh, are you okay standing up
so suddenly with your foot?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.310
Jeez, when do you think I hurt it?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.790
It was over a month ago!

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.460
It's a new year already.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.920
Don't have enough energy?

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.550
Well, why don't you eat something sweet?

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.960
Thanks, Rin-chan!

00:01:54.550 --> 00:02:00.310
Recently, I've been kinda spaced out...
Like, I keep thinking how fun the concert was...

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:01.470
I know what it is.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.270
That's called "burnout."

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.940
Huh? "Burnout"?

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.230
The big event at the end of the year is over,

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:12.070
and you don't know what
your next goal is right now.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.950
"Who am I? Where should I go?
What should I do?!"

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.830
That's the state you're in.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.240
l see!

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.490
Is that right?

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.080
This is no time to be nodding in agreement!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.630
What's important is right now and the future!

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:29.130
If you keep spacing out,
you'll stop getting work in a second!

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.590
That would be bad!

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.930
In our line of work, we're always
just a step away from unemployment!

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:38.090
For the sake of your future work,
you can't bask in your past glories!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:38.510
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.860
That's what lchigo said to me.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.560
Is that right?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:52.940
But, compared to a year ago,
I feel like I've grown a little.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:58.820
Unfortunately, you are not the one
who will decide whether or not you've grown.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:03.910
At our agency, we have an assessment
for novices under our care, like you.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.620
You know this, right?

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.410
Uh, yes, I do.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.130
Trial

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:14.470
Those who finish the training school
are treated as novices for the first two years,
Trial

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.020
a kind of trial period.
Trial

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:17.390
a kind of trial period.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:21.470
That person's work ethic, abilities, potential...

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.910
Everything about them
is examined from every angle

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:23.850
Unaccepted
Accepted

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.350
before we decide if they
can stay at Aozora Production.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.730
I heard from Atsumari...

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.240
...that there are people
whose contracts were terminated

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.690
even though they had regular work.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.700
Huh? Um, what should I do?

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.240
What should I do to stay with Aozora Pro?

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.160
It is too late to think of a countermeasure now

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.960
because they will look at the whole two years
you were a novice under our care.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.010
lchinose-san...?

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:01.010
And so, I have that the
Friday two weeks from now...

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:06.050
And just thinking about it right now
makes me feel knots in my stomach...

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.890
Assessment, huh?

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.890
Neither my agency nor Rin-chan's
has anything like that.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.400
You two are lucky...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.360
But...

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.860
But?

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.240
But I feel like that system is kind somehow.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.030
Huh?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:27.040
I mean, not many places will
watch over you for a whole two years.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.330
That means even when you didn't have work,
they were watching over you.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.550
Besides, there are some
agencies that take seiyuu,

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.550
but then keep them even
when they can't get any work.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:45.180
That's why I think firing
someone is kind, in a way.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.140
I see...

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.310
Well, think of yourself as a fish
on a plate and just get served up!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.810
What? It's a given that I'm done for?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.480
I mean, you said so yourself, didn't you?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.440
That you'd quit being a seiyuu
if you didn't pass.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.840
I did, but...

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.480
Don't worry.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:06.080
I mean, we've been working hard.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.530
If they are really watching you,
I'm sure you'll get to stay.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:12.250
Don't worry!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.410
lchigo...

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.630
But I don't know anything about
other agencies' assessment criteria,

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.500
so I'm just saying this to cheer you up.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:25.050
Jeez, you really do deserve
to be called Evil lchigo.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.350
Whoa, it's so empty!

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.720
What did I do every day back then?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.520
Your part-time job.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.440
Oh, I failed this audition.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.400
It was your first audition in a month and
a half, so you were pretty depressed, huh?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.150
Yeah, I was in so much shock I couldn't even
show my face at the office for a while...

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.210
And then Atsumari-san called you, right?

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.380
Yeah, she got mad at me.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.460
She said I needed to show my face at the office.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:02.260
I know now that she was
just trying to cheer me up.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:05.340
Futaba-san, you wandered around for an hour or two

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.720
and couldn't make up your mind to go in, huh?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.550
Su-chan, who was the same year as me,
found me and finally got me inside...

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.190
She really helped me back then.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:18.750
Su-chan

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.980
Well, speak of the devil!
Su-chan

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:20.990
Su-chan

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.550
Hello?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.460
Sunday?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.490
Yeah, I'm free!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.000
Really? Yurichin and Massu are coming, too?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:31.990
Oh, I'm so excited!

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.620
No, it's nothing.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.380
Let's talk more when we meet up.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.380
That takes me back!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.050
Atsumari-san was scary, wasn't she?

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.420
Do you remember when she lectured
while we were in training school?

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:54.850
Yeah! It wasn't just Atsumari-san, though.
All the teachers were scary.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.310
We were trained mentally thanks to that.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.230
It makes things a lot easier now.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.850
That's a leader for you!

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.940
Leader?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.270
Massu's a site leader now.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.460
Looks like she tells the young
part-timers what to do.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.040
It's nothing special.
We've just got a lot of young kids.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.490
Really? That's amazing!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.040
Remember how the teachers at
training school said to get a part-time job

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.170
because customer service
was a good way to people watch?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.880
Well, what was supposed to be part-time turned into my career...

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.380
For me, I guess the greetings were helpful.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:31.970
I didn't get to become a seiyuu,
not even a novice one,

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:37.060
but I was praised because I said
"Thank you" and "Good morning" properly.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.500
Yeah, I get that a lot, too.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.900
Anyway, who's praising you? The boy's family?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.940
Yeah, pretty much.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.440
Yurichin's engaged, you know.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.700
Huh? Engaged?

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:53.070
What a happy occasion!

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.410
Wow, congrats!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:02.340
Enough about me. Su-chan, you're going to
Kondo Agency's training school now, right?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:06.590
Yeah, but they do everything differently,
so it's really confusing.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.340
Is it really that different?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.140
Completely. I loved Aozora Pro, too,

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:16.180
but I didn't get any work at all my first year,

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.350
so I'm starting over at
an agency with less people.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.190
But I will definitely keep being a seiyuu!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.400
Yeah!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.570
We're rooting for you!

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.820
You're amazing, Su-chan...

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.910
<i>You're</i> the one who's amazing, Futaba!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.950
Huh? No, no, no, no...

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:38.580
But even in Aozora Pro,
I can't keep up with the others.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.660
I might be dropped after my assessment.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:44.300
What are you saying? I'm going to get mad.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.170
Getting into their training school
and being taken on as a novice...

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.430
You're one of the elites, Futaba. Super elite!

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.640
On top of that, you had regular roles
and a web radio show.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.300
The chance of that is one
in tens of thousands, you know.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.190
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:01.830
Yeah...
Oh, Futaba...

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:09.860
I know that I'm really blessed right
now, but it was more like luck,

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.690
and didn't have much to do with my skill...

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:15.830
Oh, but people say that luck is a skill, too...

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.450
Yeah, they do.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:22.830
In the end, my own position
isn't clear in my head.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.460
I mean, I think I can do it,
and then I think I can't...

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.280
That means you aren't
determined in your focus yet.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.760
My focus?

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:40.760
For example, where do you see yourself
in five years, ten years, thirty years...?

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.600
That's your focus.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:46.820
In thirty years?! I can't imagine that...

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.530
Does that mean you don't think
you'll be able to continue as a seiyuu?

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:54.950
Uh, no! I want to continue,
but I'm not sure if I can...

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.740
See? Your focus is wavering.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:02.250
It's not whether you <i>think</i> you can,
but whether or not you <i>want</i> to continue.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.580
I do want to continue!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.880
In what form?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.670
l-ln what form...?

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:12.540
It's said that if you can't imagine it,
then you can't make it happen.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.800
You know, they'll definitely
ask this during your assessment.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.760
What you want to become.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.230
What I want to become? Um...

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.020
If you don't even know that,
then there's no point in continuing to work.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:25.940
What?!

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.070
That's what they might say to you.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.690
They're that harsh...?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.860
That's on the nice side, you know.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:37.370
Every year, there are people who end up
crying, or are dumbfounded with shock.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.740
Is that... really true?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.200
It's true.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.420
When I accidentally go to
the office on assessment days,

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.250
there are cries of agony all around,
and I regret going in.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.580
l-l don't think I could bear it...

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:54.420
Those that get depressed just from
assessments aren't cut out to be seiyuu.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.470
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:58.100
Good morning!

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.130
Oh, it's Masumin! Great timing.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.580
G-G-G-Good night, I mean, good morning!

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.760
What's up?

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.800
Morning. Masumin, what do
you want to be in the future?
G-G-G-Good night, I mean, good morning!

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.420
l'm Ichinose Futaba from Aozora Production!
Morning. Masumin, what do
you want to be in the future?

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:10.560
Hm? Hm...

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.560
I want to be rich!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.900
Huh?

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.780
Well, see you later!

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.610
Huh?!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.780
Just as expected! She never wavers!

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.200
Isn't it obvious?

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.370
I want to be a singing,
dancing seiyuu idol princess!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.460
Wow...

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.310
What's with that reaction?
Are you making fun of me?

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:32.800
No, no, I'm moved!

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:36.970
It's amazing that you want to sing
and dance even after ten, twenty years...

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.320
You <i>are</i> making fun of me...!

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.670
No... Believe me...!
You <i>are</i> making fun of me...!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.640
No... Believe me...!

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.010
I've got my hands full with entrance exams.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:48.310
It's fine for you, Rin-chan. Your first priority should
be working hard and getting into high school.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.310
Yes!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.160
Sayo-chan is cheering me on zealously.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.660
She makes me vocabulary cards and
bakes me cookies that improve memory.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.910
Cookies that improve memory? What're those?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.460
I'll bring some to share
with you next time, lchigo-san.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:12.340
Uh... Are those okay to eat...?

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.290
Dummy, it's this way!

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.550
Really?

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:20.340
You get lost 'cause you remember
directions based on dogs and cars.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.890
Huh? But dogs are cute.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:26.390
That's not the point. You should choose
something big that doesn't move.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.230
Then you won't get lost.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.940
You should choose
something big that doesn't move!

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.820
Huh? Oh, you scared me!

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:35.610
Huh?

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.270
'Cause there was suddenly
a boy's voice right next to me.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:41.070
Futaba-san, you're good at boy voices!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.530
R-Really?

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.250
You might be better at
energetic voices than sexy ones.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.460
It must be because that's how l am.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.710
Why are you embarrassed?
It wasn't a compliment.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:51.500
Oh...

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.290
Jeez, that's why-

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.540
Now, now.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:01.000
Something big... that doesn't move...

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.720
Then I won't get lost!

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.920
Thank you... very much...

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.170
Yes, yes. Good work.
You worked hard, didn't you?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.140
We'll call you about the results later.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.930
Excuse me...

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:51.980
Assessment?

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.560
Yes! I'm Ichinose Futaba!

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.170
Good work.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:29.180
Thank you very much...

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.560
Yes, you should think
carefully about your future.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.650
Next, Ichinose.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.940
Y-Yes!

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.660
Excuse me...

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.160
Please have a seat.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.340
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.670
This feeling of being in the hot seat.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:08.380
I feel uneasy. I want something to hold on to.
I want to go into a corner.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.760
The silence is too long! It's uncomfortable!

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.690
I want to go home!

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:17.650
lchinose, what do you think about
where you are right now?

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.320
Where I am now?

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.360
Yes.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:26.320
l-l think I still have a long way to go.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:30.360
That's true. You don't have any
notable jobs other than Earphones.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.370
And you haven't in the past, either.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:36.210
There's almost no difference between
who you were and who you will become.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:42.160
I think you know this, too, lchinose, but
a list was passed out before the assessment.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:47.380
The different managers look at the list
and mark people they think will be good.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:52.430
Only two people marked your name, Ichinose.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.390
Uh... Yes...

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:59.060
In other words, in terms of hard work
and the amount and quality of jobs,

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.980
you are lacking, Ichinose.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:02.980
Yes...

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.240
Yes? You mean you admit that yourself?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.780
That might... be true...

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.200
Oh no... This is bad...

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.530
You mean there's nothing about
yourself that you think is valuable?

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.790
If that's the case, then why are you here?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.300
Huh...? Uh... I...

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.920
Huh? I can't hear you.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.040
Um, sorry...

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.800
No... I'm scared...

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.800
I can't do this!

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:40.100
Not many places will watch
over you for a whole two years.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:45.020
It's not whether you <i>think</i> you can,
but whether or not you <i>want</i> to continue.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.280
Then here's a question for you:

00:16:56.140 --> 00:17:02.590
If you could continue as a seiyuu,
what kind of seiyuu do you want to become?

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.440
I...

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.230
You should choose something big
that doesn't move.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.960
I want to become a seiyuu
who works for a long time.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:12.350
Oh?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:19.940
I'm plain, and not particularly good-looking.

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:26.710
To me, the selling point of Ichinose Futaba
is the part of me that's bold, and a little slow.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:29.280
Even if times are hard, I won't lose heart.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:33.660
Uh, in that respect,
I'm stronger than I thought.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:37.200
Using that strength, I want to
continue being a seiyuu for a long time!

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:42.580
I wonder if you know just
how ambitious that sounds?

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:48.960
Even the young seiyuu who are suddenly
chosen as heroines and have a lot of big parts

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.130
rapidly get less work as they near thirty.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.120
To say you want to work
for a long time in that world

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.140
might be harder than saying
you want to play a heroine.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:06.630
Even so, that doesn't change the desire
I have to continue working for a long time.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:11.900
Of course, I would be happy to play
the main character or a heroine,

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:17.650
but even if it's just a short line,
I want to make those watching laugh or cry...

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:21.370
I want to be a seiyuu that people remember

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.710
and keep working for a long time.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.250
Please allow me to continue working with you.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:48.190
After this, we will discuss the matter
in the office and contact you.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.900
Okay. Um...

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.240
Thank you for everything up to now.

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:57.690
lchinose-san!

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:02.500
I like the boy characters you play!

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.340
I want to hear more of them!

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.960
Thank you very much.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.930
No matter what happens after this,
I'll do my best!

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:25.180
Hey! Futaba!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.920
Good work-daberry!

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.150
"-Daberry"?

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:32.280
You don't get it-daberry?

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.570
N-No...

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:36.770
Then, what about "Good work-chi"?
Does that work better-chi?

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:42.490
Um, even if you ask me if it's "better-chi?"
I still don't know what's going on-chi...

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:47.790
Actually, I'll be providing the voice
for a local mascot starting in the spring!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.950
And guess what? It's a strawberry character!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.710
Wow! That's great, Ichigo!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:56.050
For stuff like this, it's important
to create a memorable character, right?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.050
Can you think of anything catchy?

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.300
A strawberry character...

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.550
What about using the "go" from "ichigo"
for "go-go-go"? How's that, go-go-go?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.310
"Go-go-go" ? Sounds menacing!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:10.500
Oh, it's Rin-chan.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.930
I wonder how her entrance exam went.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.190
I think Rin-chan will be fine, but...

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.020
Rin-chan!

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:22.700
Over here!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.790
Oh, good...

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.250
Yes, this is Ichinose.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.840
This is Atsumari from Aozora Production.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:42.010
I'm calling to tell you the assessment results.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.500
Yes...

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:51.020
In other words, I could not move up
to associate member of the agency...

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.900
D-Does that mean...?

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.880
Futaba...

00:20:58.880 --> 00:20:59.970
Futaba-san...!

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:05.990
I can stay...? I can stay, right...?

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:11.240
Yes, sorry, the decision's been deferred, then?

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:14.230
lchinose, do you really understand?

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:18.380
"Deferred" means you are getting
a grace period of another year.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:21.000
Please work hard during this time.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:26.390
And at the next assessment,
you really will be held responsible for

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.850
your attitude toward work
and the results of that.

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.510
Yes, I understand!

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:36.020
Let's both work hard so you can become
a seiyuu who works for a long time.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.070
Thank you very much!

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:50.030
Rin-chan... lchigo...

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:53.020
Yay!

00:21:54.810 --> 00:22:00.650
kono de te mirai wo kaerunda chousen shiyou yo
Let's try changing the future with these hands

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:05.970
hikari no saki e tobidasou
Let's fly to the end of the light

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:14.640
arata no suteeji e tobidashita kedo ne
Even though we flew to a new stage

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:16.380
Congrats on graduating
arata no suteeji e tobidashita kedo ne
Even though we flew to a new stage

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:18.240
arata no suteeji e tobidashita kedo ne
Even though we flew to a new stage

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:23.800
tachi wa tagaru kabe jouzu mae ni susumenai
There's a wall blocking the way, and we can't move forward

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:28.790
norikoeta saki ni egao ga aru nara
But if there are smiles waiting when we climb over it

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:34.660
donna tsurai shiren demo ganbatte miru yo
Then we'll do our best no matter how difficult the trials

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:36.940
genjitsutte kibishii...
Reality is harsh...

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:39.850
dakara gooru wa mabushii
That's why the goal is blindingly bright

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:44.900
akiramecha dame da!
Don't give up!

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:51.340
omoikitte yuuki dashite dekiru koto zenbu yatte mireba
If we draw up all our courage and try doing everything we can

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:56.150
mirai wa irodzuki kagayaku
Then the future will take on color and sparkle

00:22:56.150 --> 00:22:58.900
gamusharatte tsutawarunda
People can tell when we work hard

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:01.080
daremo mitenai tokoro demo
Even if we do it when no one's around

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:03.060
Okay, let's start recording!
daremo mitenai tokoro demo
Even if we do it when no one's around

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:09.490
tobira no mukou deaeru egao no tame ni
We do it for the smiles we'll meet on the other side of the door

00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:19.500
We're seiyuu, and that's what it means to work as a seiyuu.

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:26.500
Yay, good work today, Earphones!

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.510
Something's in the works...
and it's gonna be huge!

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:31.700
What?

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:32.510
This!

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.550
What?!

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.490
What...?!
